+# Starlight Social Media Team OS
+
+Created: 2026-06-26
+
+Status: internal operating system. Nothing in this document approves external
+publishing, scheduling, customer messages, spend, deploys, merges, Slack access
+changes, or Hermes gateway activation.
+
+## Purpose
+
+Build a guarded, high-taste social production system for FrankX, AI-Architect,
+Builder Education, GenCreator, Tooling, and selected Starlight portfolio lanes.
+
+The system turns signals into durable assets:
+
+```text
+Signal -> brief -> deterministic asset -> QA -> Slack proof -> approval packet
+  -> human decision -> manual publish/schedule -> performance learning
+```
+
+The team optimizes for founder-useful proof, not content volume.
+
+## Current Audit
+
+### 2026-06-26 Correction
+
+The first carousel proved the mechanics but did not meet Frank's social-team
+quality bar. Treat it as a learning artifact, not as a model to copy.
+
+New rule: the social team does not route carousel candidates to
+`#social-approvals` unless the asset passes the V2 carousel social-confidence
+gate at 90/100 or higher. A complete file packet is not enough. The work must be
+something a competent social/design team would be willing to stand behind
+publicly.
+
+### Existing Strengths
+
+- `ecosystem.json` already defines brand rooms, channel IDs, approval gates, and
+  hard external-action boundaries.
+- `SLACK_AUTOMATION_EXECUTION_LAYER_2026-06-25.md` clearly separates Slack,
+  GitHub, Vercel/domain truth, Hermes runtime, and Codex synthesis.
+- `CAROUSEL_FACTORY_OPERATING_SYSTEM_2026-06-25.md` gives the carousel lane a
+  focused channel, required pack files, and deterministic deck standard.
+- `SOCIAL_IMAGE_GENERATION_CONTENT_WORKFLOWS_2026-06-22.md` already names the
+  correct split: generated images for concepts and deterministic layouts for
+  exact text.
+- The first carousel pack has real artifacts: `BRIEF.md`, `DESIGN.md`,
+  `TASTE.md`, `POST.md`, `index.html`, `deck.pdf`, `cover-preview.png`, and
+  `evidence.json`.
+
+### Overbuilt Or Risky
+
+- The design standards are very strict. Keep the gates, but daily social output
+  should use a small evidence packet instead of heavyweight process theater.
+- Slack can become noisy if every draft is posted top-level. Use top-level posts
+  only for `Brief`, `Draft`, `Proof`, `Approval`, and `Learning`; keep variants
+  in threads.
+- The current Agentic Coding OS carousel risks making Slack look mandatory. The
+  stronger client/community template is "operating spaces": Slack channels,
+  Discord channels, Linear projects, Notion databases, ChatGPT projects, Claude
+  projects, Codex threads, GitHub branches, and app workspaces all serve the same
+  routing concept.
+
+### Cut
+
+- Cut generic AI-gradient visual language.
+- Cut text-heavy generated images.
+- Cut fake dashboards and fake product logos.
+- Cut automatic platform variants when the core artifact is not excellent.
+- Cut any claim that Hermes gateways, publishing bots, or autonomous public
+  action are live unless the proof exists.
+
+### Missing
+
+- Brand/lane social foundations for FrankX, AI-Architect, and Builder Education.
+- A reusable approval packet template with claim risk, AI disclosure, source
+  proof, media paths, and explicit decision language.
+- A learning loop that reads prior approvals/rejections, performance, design QA,
+  brand style guides, and current AI lab updates before choosing the next
+  carousel.
+- A lightweight standard template that can be reused for clients and community
+  members.
+
+## Roles
+
+| Role | Owner | Job | Output |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Social Commander | Codex + Frank approval | Route signals, choose one focused asset, enforce gates | daily/weekly production plan |
+| Brand Editor | brand room owner | Fit angle to FrankX, AI-Architect, GenCreator, Tooling, or Starlight | voice and audience decision |
+| Research Scout | Codex/research profile | Verify AI lab, platform, product, and source claims | source list and claim-risk labels |
+| Carousel Producer | Codex | Build exact text decks in HTML/SVG/Figma/Canva-style systems | deck pack and export |
+| Visual Director | design-intelligence lane | Choose generated-image vs deterministic method and score output | QA notes and 30-point score |
+| Approval Steward | Codex + human | Package final candidate and ask for decision | approval packet in `#social-approvals` |
+| Learning Analyst | Codex automation | Capture approvals, rejections, performance, and QA patterns | learning note for next run |
+
+## Slack Channels
+
+| Channel | Use | Do Not Use For |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `#social-command` (`C0BB6K4U4MT`) | planning, platform routing, weekly content queue | final approvals |
+| `#social-carousels` (`C0BCPG55PJB`) | carousel briefs, deck proofs, QA, draft packets | publishing or scheduling |
+| `#social-approvals` (`C0BB6K6TT1B`) | final human approval gate | ideation chatter |
+| `#content-film-prep` (`C0BCJ0MNLKS`) | recording briefs, hooks, beats, B-roll needs | design QA |
+| `#design-intelligence` (`C0B9W4TE5K5`) | reusable design QA, visual standards, generated asset critique | brand-only copy edits |
+| `#daily-report` (`C0BBHBAQZMH`) | executive proof and meaningful risks | low-level draft iteration |
+| `#brand-frankx` (`C0BBP3AJ39T`) | FrankX positioning and POV | cross-brand routing |
+| `#brand-ai-coe` (`C0BCLPDGHAL`) | AI-Architect / enterprise / Oracle CoE angle | consumer creator content |
+| `#brand-creator-systems` (`C0BBSFAJKDG`) | GenCreator and creator OS packaging | enterprise-only approvals |
+| `#brand-tooling-oss` (`C0BCLPGJ3RN`) | open-source/tooling trust content | customer messages |
+
+## Approval Gates
+
+Agents may research, draft, generate internal artifacts, inspect outputs, run
+local checks, summarize, create approval packets, and post internal proof.
+
+Human approval is required before:
+
+- publishing or scheduling social posts
+- sending customer or partner messages
+- deploying or promoting production
+- merging to main
+- spending money or activating vendors
+- changing access, channel membership, DNS, or domains
+- starting Hermes gateways or autonomous profile runtimes
+
+Approval language must request one of:
+
+- `APPROVE`
+- `APPROVE WITH EDITS: <edit>`
+- `REVISE: <reason>`
+- `HOLD`
+
+## Content Lanes
+
+| Lane | Brand | Primary Audience | Typical Artifact |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Founder AI OS | FrankX | founders and operators | LinkedIn carousel, post, short script |
+| AI-Architect | AI CoE | enterprise AI leaders and partners | governance carousel, architecture diagram |
+| Builder Education | FrankX / Tooling / GenCreator | builders using Codex, Claude Code, ChatGPT, GitHub | tutorial carousel, setup guide |
+| Creator Systems | GenCreator | creators and creator-led teams | workflow carousel, template pack |
+| Portfolio Ops | Starlight / FrankX | multi-brand operators | operating map, proof digest |
+| Design Intelligence | Starlight / Arcanea | builders and visual teams | QA rubric, visual case study |
+
+## Cadence
+
+Daily:
+
+1. Read new signals from AI labs, platform changes, Slack approvals, repo proof,
+   design QA, and prior performance.
+2. Pick at most one carousel candidate unless there is a major update.
+3. Build or revise one durable asset pack.
+4. Post concise proof to `#social-carousels`.
+5. Route approval-ready candidates to `#social-approvals`.
+6. If there is no meaningful output, do not manufacture noise.
+
+Weekly:
+
+1. Review approved, rejected, revised, held, and ignored packets.
+2. Review performance if posts were manually published.
+3. Promote the best pack into a reusable client/community template.
+4. Cut stale lanes, duplicated variants, and weak platform assumptions.
+5. Update brand guides when Frank's approvals reveal a pattern.
+
+## Asset Formats
+
+| Asset | Best Format | Where It Lives |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Source brief | Markdown | repo pack |
+| Brand/style guide | Markdown | repo foundation docs |
+| Exact carousel slides | HTML/CSS, SVG, Figma, Canva, or slides | repo and/or design tool |
+| LinkedIn document carousel | PDF | repo pack and Slack file when routed |
+| Instagram carousel | PNG sequence | repo pack or Canva export |
+| Cover concept | PNG/WebP generated image, inspected | repo `docs/visuals/` or pack assets |
+| Diagram | SVG/HTML/Figma | repo pack |
+| Approval packet | Markdown plus Slack summary | repo pack and `#social-approvals` |
+| Performance note | Markdown/JSON | repo pack or weekly learning ledger |
+
+## What Belongs Where
+
+### Slack
+
+Slack is the visible cockpit: routing, proof, approvals, decisions, short
+updates, and learning summaries. It is not the canonical long-term asset store.
+
+Use Slack for:
+
+- concise proof updates
+- approval requests
+- final decision receipts
+- design QA findings that should become reusable
+- performance learning summaries
+
+### Repo
+
+The repo is durable truth.
+
+Use the repo for:
+
+- briefs
+- source links
+- deterministic deck source
+- approval packets
+- evidence and QA notes
+- reusable brand/lane foundations
+- learning ledgers and automation registry
+
+### Canva
+
+Use Canva when:
+
+- a human needs easy editing after the deterministic source exists
+- a campaign needs many manually adjusted variants
+- brand kits, social scheduling handoff, or team review in a familiar tool matter
+- the artifact is more marketing package than code-native system
+
+Do not use Canva as the only source of truth for exact technical diagrams,
+claim tracking, or automation-readable evidence.
+
+### Local HTML/SVG/PDF
+
+Use local deterministic production when:
+
+- exact text, slide numbers, diagrams, or channel names matter
+- the output should be reproducible and diffable
+- the deck needs PDF export for LinkedIn
+- the pack should become a client/community template
+
+### Generated Image Assets
+
+Use image generation for:
+
+- cinematic covers
+- visual metaphors
+- thumbnails
+- mood frames
+- campaign art
+- non-text-heavy scene concepts
+
+Do not use generated images for final exact slide text, final diagrams, product
+UI claims, logos, source citations, or dense labels.
+
+The local imagegen skill says the built-in `image_gen` tool is the default for
+normal raster generation. CLI/model-specific behavior must be checked in the
+current local skill and official docs before relying on it. The Social Media
+Team OS should not depend on a specific model name such as GPT Image 2; it
+depends on the method: brief, generate, inspect, critique, iterate, approve.
+
+## Image Generation + HTML/Canva Workflow
+
+1. Write the outcome contract: audience, surface, first read, proof, failure
+   modes, and acceptance gate.
+2. Decide production method:
+   - exact text/data/UI/diagram: deterministic HTML/SVG/Figma/Canva
+   - cinematic cover or metaphor: generated image plus inspection
+   - editable campaign family: deterministic source first, Canva variant second
+3. For generated images, write a short art direction prompt with final crop,
+   brand tokens, subject, composition, and avoid list.
+4. Inspect the actual output. Reject fake text, fake logos, malformed UI,
+   private data, weak crop, artifacts, or generic prompt style.
+5. Add exact overlay text outside the generator when needed.
+6. Export final assets and record paths, prompt, QA score, and approval gate.
+
+## Learning Loop
+
+The daily carousel factory must learn before producing:
+
+- AI lab updates from official sources only when topical claims are made
+- prior approval decisions from `#social-approvals`
+- prior design QA scores from `#design-intelligence` and pack `evidence.json`
+- prior performance when manually published posts have metrics
+- brand-specific guides in `starlight-design-intelligence` and this docs tree
+- Frank's direct edits, especially headline, stack, tone, and claim-risk edits
+
+Minimum learning note per carousel:
+
+```text
+Learning input:
+- latest official source signal:
+- prior approval/rejection signal:
+- design QA signal:
+- performance signal:
+- brand guide signal:
+
+Decision:
+- make:
+- cut:
+- carry forward:
+```
+
+## Standard Client/Community Template
+
+The reusable template is:
+
+```text
+1. Brand/lane social guide
+2. Carousel style guide
+3. Post voice guide
+4. Image generation guide
+5. Approval packet template
+6. One sample carousel pack
+7. One weekly learning ledger
+```
+
+This is the client/community version of the OS: enough structure to protect
+quality and approvals, not enough process to bury the team.
+
