+# Instagram Variant: Agentic Coding OS
+
+Created: 2026-06-26
+
+Status: platform adaptation plan. Not published, not scheduled, not a new
+approval candidate.
+
+## Decision
+
+Use the current LinkedIn deck as the source of truth. For Instagram, cut the
+slide text by roughly 35-45 percent and keep one mechanism per slide. Do not
+post the LinkedIn PDF as-is to Instagram.
+
+## Platform Goal
+
+Make the same idea legible in a fast mobile feed:
+
+- one clean hook
+- one operating concept per slide
+- fewer tool names
+- more concrete proof language
+- no tiny source or governance copy on image slides
+- source links and claim context move to caption/approval packet
+
+## Slide Copy Adaptation
+
+| Slide | Instagram copy | Keep / cut |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| 1 | Build an operating system for your AI agents. | Keep the current hook. |
+| 2 | Treat agents like teammates, not magic prompts. | Cut lab/product detail. |
+| 3 | Loose prompts create loose work. | Keep the risk, reduce examples. |
+| 4 | Give each layer one job: space, truth, proof, approval, learning. | Merge stack details. |
+| 5 | The loop: brief -> work -> verify -> proof. | Keep as the core diagram. |
+| 6 | Agents prepare. Humans approve irreversible moves. | Keep the guardrail. |
+| 7 | Write the work order: outcome, context, boundary, proof. | Keep as a saveable template. |
+| 8 | The labs are moving fast. Operators need governance. | Move named sources to caption. |
+| 9 | Start with five spaces: status, intake, execution, truth, approval. | Keep, shorten labels. |
+| 10 | Save this before your next agent build session. | Stronger Instagram CTA. |
+
+## Instagram Caption
+
+AI agents are becoming teammates.
+
+But teammates need lanes, ownership, proof, and review.
+
+The operating model:
+
+- intake
+- workspace
+- truth
+- proof
+- approval
+- learning
+
+Slack can be one cockpit. GitHub can be source truth. Codex, Claude Code, and
+other agents can handle different parts of the work.
+
+The important part is not the tool list.
+
+The important part is the system: what each agent owns, where work happens, how
+proof is checked, and when a human must approve the next move.
+
+Save this before your next agent build session.
+
+## Claim Risk
+
+Medium.
+
+Keep source-backed claims in caption or approval notes. Do not overpack the
+image slides with named lab updates, product claims, or enterprise claims.
+
+## Approval Gate
+
+This variant can be used only after the existing `Agentic Coding OS` approval
+candidate receives `APPROVE` or `APPROVE WITH EDITS`. If Frank wants Instagram
+first, export a separate PNG sequence from this copy before publishing.
