+# Taste Review - Founder Operating Room
+
+## Verdict
+
+Pass with notes: 28/30.
+
+This is stronger as a workroom proof and future approval candidate than as another immediate approval post. It carries Frank's positive direction: grateful, constructive, specific, and founder-to-founder.
+
+## Score
+
+| Criterion | Score | Notes |
+| --- | ---: | --- |
+| First read and hierarchy | 5/5 | Cover states the aspiration quickly. |
+| Brand fit and distinctiveness | 5/5 | Tactile founder operating room feels FrankX / Starlight, not generic AI. |
+| Craft, typography, spacing, composition | 4/5 | Strong overall; a Figma/Canva kerning pass could improve final flagship polish. |
+| Accessibility and surface fit | 4/5 | 4:5 contact sheet reads well; some supporting labels are small. |
+| Accuracy, provenance, no artifacts | 5/5 | Exact text is deterministic; generated source frames avoid readable fake labels. |
+| Usefulness for intended surface | 5/5 | Clear reusable operating model and caption. |
+
+## What Works
+
+- Positive hook avoids lazy fear framing.
+- The operating model is concrete: cockpit, agent jobs, proof, content studio, approval, learning.
+- The art direction feels like an editorial campaign rather than a generic SaaS carousel.
+- The pack is now reusable across Instagram and LinkedIn review.
+
+## What To Cut
+
+- Do not add more approval queue noise until the current queue is decided.
+- Do not over-explain Slack as the whole strategy; keep it as one cockpit implementation.
+- Do not claim autonomous public action or live gateways.
+
+## Carry Forward
+
+- Use generated images only as text-free scene foundations.
+- Keep exact typography deterministic.
+- Keep approval gates explicit.
+- Keep positive founder language when the topic is agentic operations.
