+- YouTube requires creators to disclose AI-generated or meaningfully altered realistic content, including generated realistic scenes that did not occur: https://support.google.com/youtube/answer/14328491
+- LinkedIn supports document posts from PDFs and recommends PDF conversion where possible; files cannot exceed 100MB or 300 pages and videos/animations in documents render as static: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/a518909
+- FTC endorsement guidance requires clear material-connection disclosures when there is a financial, employment, personal, or family relationship with a brand; disclosures must be hard to miss and placed with the endorsement: https://www.ftc.gov/business-guidance/resources/disclosures-101-social-media-influencers
+- OpenAI image generation supports generation, edits, and multi-turn iterative image workflows; production use still needs prompt, critique, edit, brand QA, export, and approval: https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/image-generation
