+# Social Approval Backlog - 2026-06-26
+
+Status: internal approval queue evaluation. No public posting or scheduling was
+performed.
+
+## Why This Matters
+
+The social system is now producing better assets than the approval queue can
+absorb. That is not a content problem. It is a decision-throughput problem.
+
+The right move is fewer candidates, clearer choices, and stronger replacement
+logic.
+
+## Live Queue
+
+| Candidate | Status | Recommendation | Reason |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Revised Agentic Coding OS carousel | Approval-ready, 27/30 | Decide first | Most complete LinkedIn educational candidate; incorporates feedback that Slack is one cockpit, not the whole OS. |
+| Original Agentic Coding OS carousel | Superseded draft, 26/30 | Hold or archive | Revised version is stronger and more accurate. |
+| Agentic Portfolio OS carousel | Draft candidate | Revise or hold | Older negative framing and Slack-first model are weaker than current doctrine. |
+| Founder Operating Room carousel | Workroom proof, 28/30 | Promote only if it replaces one waiting item | Strong positive frame and emotional/business story; should not add to backlog without replacing another candidate. |
+
+## Recommended Decision Order
+
+1. Decide revised Agentic Coding OS.
+2. Mark original Agentic Coding OS as superseded unless explicitly preferred.
+3. Hold Agentic Portfolio OS until rewritten with the positive hook doctrine.
+4. Promote Founder Operating Room only if Frank wants it as the next public
+   candidate.
+
+## Approval Language To Use
+
+```text
+APPROVE
+APPROVE WITH EDITS: <edit>
+REVISE: <reason>
+HOLD
+REPLACE: Founder Operating Room replaces <candidate>
+```
+
+## Guardrail
+
+Do not add more approval candidates until one of the current candidates is
+approved, held, replaced, or archived.
+
+## Slack Route
+
+Post to `#social-approvals` as a queue hygiene note, not as a new publication
+candidate.
